troski":false,"_score_piotroski":44.4,"_gate_spread":0.09695194807321743,"_gp_spread":true,"_score_spread":48.5,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.2720409380890684,"_gp_roic_consistency":true,"_score_roic_consistency":54.7,"_gate_incr_roic":0.46866731710287846,"_gp_incr_roic":true,"_score_incr_roic":100.0,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.021733258954851523,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":40.6,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":0.0077334730246241545,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":57.7,"_gate_fund_growth":0,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.16192853492305,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":100.0,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.0014920919128618322,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":97.5,"_gate_insider_own":0.0047999998,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":3.2,"_gate_insider_buying":0.5,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":50.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Core & Main, Inc. engages in the distribution of water, wastewater, storm drainage, and fire protection products and related services in the United States. The company's products portfolio include pipes, valves, hydrants, fittings, and other products and services used for service, repair and replacement of underground water infrastructure; storm drainage products, such as corrugated HDPE and metal piping systems, retention basins, inline drains, manholes, grates, geosynthetics, erosion control, and other related products; fire protection products, including fire protection pipes, valves, fittings, sprinkler heads and other accessories, as well as fabrication and kitting services; smart meter products; and smart metering solutions which include meter accessories, meter installation, network infrastructure and software installation, training, and long-term services, as well as engineered treatment plant products. Its specialty products and services are used in the maintenance, repair, replacement, and construction of water, wastewater, storm drainage, and fire protection infrastructure. The company serves municipalities, private water companies, and professional contractors in the municipal, non-residential, and residential end markets. Core & Main, Inc. was founded in 1874 and is headquartered in Saint Louis, Missouri.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Mark R. Witkowski CPA | CEO & Director | Age 50 | Compensation: $1.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 5K people. Revenue per employee of $1.2M ranks in the top quartile among Industrials peers, with revenue growing 16%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $184K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Core & Main, Inc. is a mid-cap industrials business with a $8.3B market cap on $6.7B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +16% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 19% against a 9% cost of capital \u2014 a 10-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat, with gross margins sitting at 27%.","The business throws off $1.0B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 15 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.88\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 9.1\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 16.2% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.3% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 6% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 38% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Growing faster than most Industrials peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Core & Main (NYSE: CNM) trims EBITDA outlook but buys back a record $171 million","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/core-main-nyse-cnm-trims-ebitda-outlook-but-buys-back-a-record-171-million.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":179459396